Notebook[{
Cell["HypergraphRule", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"e035ef9b-7f01-9e4c-ab95-4f7003d55b65"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"HypergraphRule", "[", 
    RowBox[{"input", ",", " ", "output"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"5741fca6-5a1e-ff4e-b35e-b52e17603a42"],
 " ",
 "represents the rewrite rule taking the hypergraph input to the hypergraph \
output."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"0382c092-fa6f-ae4c-9d4a-4d660e769159"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"277caaa9-0239-7b42-a5eb-12b8d33a4a64"],

Cell["\<\
Either side may be given as anything Hypergraph accepts, and is converted; a \
side that is not a hypergraph gives HypergraphRule::hg.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b13222bf-1ebb-a64a-9a7e-0ca84c41dcdc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"rule", "[", "hg", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"945615be-9824-4f48-951e-b91c56329237"],
 " applies the rule, giving one event for every way the input matches. See ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphRuleApply", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"b53e8efb-0e66-c744-88fb-23aa568fc439"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"894cf6bf-be0e-614e-98d2-226a51200a4d"],

Cell["\<\
A vertex of the input that the output keeps is carried through the rewrite; \
one the output introduces is created fresh; one the output drops is \
destroyed. \"SharedVertices\", \"NewVertices\" and \"DeletedVertices\" report \
the three groups, read off the two sides by vertex identifier.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a29dd79b-5373-9945-bc2d-258c93e62e89"],

Cell["\<\
Vertices correspond between the two sides by identifier, so the same name on \
both sides means the same vertex, and a name on the output alone means a new \
one.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"068ddb39-9079-5747-8d3b-c41f4d03a011"],

Cell["\<\
The shape follows the reference paclet this package grew out of, so that \
rules written for that one read the same here.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c5beaa50-ee1a-6a46-9a94-5f18663ea409"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"b2fa054f-818c-2e49-a0ec-8cea98b534ba"],

Cell["\<\
Subdividing an edge: the two endpoints are kept, a third vertex is new.\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"52bfefa4-2172-3148-aa1c-9fde304d3b26"],

Cell["sub = HypergraphRule[{{1, 2}}, {{1, 3}, {3, 2}}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9c9a1173-4a14-bd44-923d-47b93ed2c6b4"],

